lmux's changes to libghostty (ghostty-org/ghostty at GHOSTTY_COMMIT), applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh.

Release idle GPU memory: an unfocused surface that hasn't drawn for 3 s releases its swap chain
(atlas copies, cell buffers, the render targets but the one last presented, which the layer keeps
showing: releasing it would empty its IOSurface) and its Metal command queue. On Apple silicon
(macOS 26) the process's first GPU submission makes Metal set up ~80-110 MB of driver memory that
lives as long as the queue that submitted it: with every surface idle it is freed. The next frame
rebuilds both (~3 ms), the same path a surface takes when it becomes visible again. The focused
surface keeps everything (the next key pays nothing), and so does a surface whose frames fail.
Files: src/renderer/{Metal,generic,Thread}.zig.

No per-thread alternate signal stack (std_options.signal_stack_size = null, src/main_ghostty.zig):
Zig's default puts 256 KB in every thread's TLS, 5 threads per pane. Without it the Sentry/Zig
handlers can't run on a stack overflow in a libghostty thread; macOS still writes the crash report.
Program status (OSC 7501) to the embedder: Ghostty parses it but dropped it in termio
(`.program_status => {}`). Now a report (state, blocked kind, app name) reaches the apprt as
GHOSTTY_ACTION_PROGRAM_STATUS; queries still get no reply. Codex's TUI reports its state this way
in its own terminal, which lmux uses as each pane's Codex status. Files: include/ghostty.h,
src/apprt/{action,surface}.zig, src/termio/stream_handler.zig, src/Surface.zig.

Input method caret in the preedit (ghostty_surface_preedit_caret): the host passes the IME's caret
as a UTF-8 byte offset with the preedit text, and the renderer draws a bar cursor before that
codepoint when it is inside the preedit (moving through a Chinese or Japanese composition with the
arrow keys); at either end nothing is drawn, as before. Files: include/ghostty.h, src/Surface.zig,
src/apprt/embedded.zig, src/renderer/{State,generic}.zig.

Every change is marked "lmux:".

